<p>Pope Leo XIV returned to Rome on Thursday after wrapping up an 11-day, four-country trip across Africa. The tour ended in Equatorial Guinea, where he celebrated an open-air Mass in Malabo after visiting a prison in Bata. He traveled through Algeria, Cameroon, Angola and Equatorial Guinea. Several outlets described the journey as a landmark visit by the first American pope, blending large public worship events with unusually direct criticism of war, corruption and inequality.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yJ9RJpz2Phs3Bkc07YABaFwK8b1vtAXtav6PGyz04bxku7gkFa-Khv0OAcibwH5IK8TNhze5Bb7Vc7fOqdJnen-FyFwG6yZ9iwFYcAsHsivYfTmU9PB68TMjZXFQNnUpUCjWdgldvR9e2mOo1--m92i-UwYC_evCgPYyo11mlon4QL6NR5EXBaWXVzqjBhEdpsxzwe00cizh8-8odYRDto1tL1q3ThH1ZYW-UmeXQS_zgkQXxIkGyCp9UrH6_0hXD11dq5dzPOffqmeC8g' alt='Pope Leo XIV arrives to celebrate the Holy Mass at the Malabo stadium, in Equatorial Guinea, on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Prison message: At a prison in Bata, Leo told inmates that “life is not defined solely by one’s mistakes,” making rehabilitation and hope central themes of his final stop in Equatorial Guinea.</li><li>Sharp rhetoric: Several outlets said Leo used unusually frank language throughout the trip, criticizing outside powers he said were breaking international law in Africa and beyond.</li><li>Trump feud: Several reports tied Leo’s appeals for peace to an ongoing public clash with President Trump over the war in Iran, giving the visit broader geopolitical visibility.</li><li>Historic first: PBS called the journey a “visit for the history books,” underscoring Africa’s importance as a major stage in the early papacy of the first American pontiff.</li></ul><blockquote>Life is not defined solely by one’s mistakes - Pope Leo XIV</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: Leo cast dialogue, unity and peace as the practical answer to war and inequality, and urged political leaders to put people before power. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-stressed-importance-of-dialogue-on-africa-trip/a-76906045'>DW</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: The BBC said the pope’s closing speech on prisons was frank and passionate, in keeping with a tour marked by direct public criticism rather than cautious diplomatic language. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c80m4822m1no'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>PBS assessment: PBS framed the journey as historically significant for the Vatican, highlighting both its sweep across four countries and the visibility of Leo’s peace message. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/pope-wraps-up-an-africa-visit-for-the-history-books-with-a-mass-in-equatorial-guinea'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/pope-leo-heading-back-to-rome-after-outspoken-africa-tour'>Pope Leo heading back to Rome after outspoken Africa tour</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-pope-leo-africa-tour-equatorial-guinea/'>Pope Leo wraps up Africa tour which saw him feud with Trump and blast ‘tyrants’</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/pope-wraps-up-an-africa-visit-for-the-history-books-with-a-mass-in-equatorial-guinea'>Pope wraps up an Africa visit for the history books with a Mass in Equatorial Guinea</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/22/world/africa/pope-leo-equatorial-guinea.html'>Pope Leo, Visiting African Prison, Urges Inmates to Find Hope Amid Despair</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-stressed-importance-of-dialogue-on-africa-trip/a-76906045'>Pope Leo stressed importance of dialogue on Africa trip</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/04/23/pope-leo-xiv-ends-africa-tour-with-open-air-mass-in-equatorial-guinea'>Pope Leo XIV ends Africa tour with open-air mass in Equatorial Guinea</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c80m4822m1no'>Pope 